{
  "title": "Logo pattern phone cases: black TPU with lime plugs",
  "summary": "Four everyday phone cases in black TPU with the Try New Things logo in lime PLA: Halftone (one giant logo in dots) for a Xiaomi 12T Pro and an iPhone 13 mini, Echo (the smile rippling out) for an iPhone 13 mini and an iPhone 14 Pro Max.",
  "status": "approved",
  "date": "2026-11-27",
  "material": "Black TPU 95A cases (Gås), lime PLA plug plates (TNT)",
  "notes": "How it works: the outer 1.8 mm of the TPU back is a lattice with the pattern cut through it; a lime PLA plate lies in a pocket inside the back and its plugs fill the openings, 0.1 mm below the face. The phone holds the plate in; to take it out, lift it at the fingernail notch at the bottom end. Case shell (fit, lip, button covers, ports, corner bumpers, camera hole) from the rig-kit cases. Plates: Gås 11 h 21 min, 101 g black TPU 95A (3 walls, Arachne, reduce crossing walls), all 4 cases, overnight, reboot first; TNT 3 h 17 min, 77 g lime PLA at 230 C / 12 mm3/s, 0.16 mm, 15 % infill, concentric top surface. No supports. Round 1 review by four independent reviewers: all PASS WITH CHANGES, no blockers; their quick fixes are in (removal notch, round ripple ends, filled halftone webs, straight halftone edges, smaller plug gaps, lead-ins). Fit coupons skipped by choice. Known: no reliable wireless charging or MagSafe through the 3-4.7 mm back; PLA plates soften in a hot car; 12T Pro data from photos (+-2.5 mm).",
